# Disambiguate the `Post` record constructor from the ambient `Http.Post`
# constructor.
#
# `State.Post` is this app's 8-field record alias. Ipê also ships `HttpMethod`
# (`Get | Post | Put | ...`) whose nullary `Post` constructor is reachable
# unqualified in the prelude, so the bare `Post` in `init`'s seed list resolves
# to the HTTP verb (a nullary value), not the record constructor — surfacing as
# IPE-T0001 "expected an 8-arg function, found HttpMethod". Qualify the five
# seed-post constructions as `State.Post` so they bind to the record alias
# unambiguously. (The underlying resolver precedence — an imported user
# constructor losing to an ambient qualified-home builtin — is tracked
# upstream; qualifying is the idiomatic disambiguation regardless.)

# `Web.app`'s `view` is `Model -> Element Msg`; the framework applies
# `Ui.layout` internally. The upstream declares `view : Model -> any` and calls
# `Ui.layout` itself, returning `Html` — the wildcard return unifies with the
# shape's `Element` requirement at type-check but the emit re-wraps the `Html`
# in `ui_layout`, so the emitted crate fails to compile (E0308: expected
# `Element`, found `Html`). Return the inner `Element` (the framework applies
# the empty-attr layout) and declare the honest `Element Msg` type.
[[edit]]
file: src/Main.ipe
find:
"""
view : Model -> any
view model =
    Ui.layout
        []
        (Ui.column
"""
replace:
"""
view : Model -> Element Msg
view model =
    Ui.column
"""

[[edit]]
file: src/Main.ipe
find:
"""
            [ topNav model, pageBody model, pageFooter ])
"""
replace:
"""
            [ topNav model, pageBody model, pageFooter ]
"""

[[edit]]
